🧠 Remember:

Task still running  → isDone() → false
Task finished       → isDone() → true

And:

isDone() only checks; it does not wait.

When the main thread calls get(), the main thread waits until the task is complete. After the task completes, get() returns the task's result
(if there is one). Then isDone() checks whether the task is complete, so it returns true.

Main Thread
    ↓
future.get()
    ↓
Waits
    ↓
Task completes
    ↓
get() returns result
    ↓
isDone()
    ↓
true
-------------
For a task with no return value:

future.get();

just waits for completion; there is no result to retrieve.
---------------------
1. isDone() → false

Here we check while the task is still running:

Future<?> future = pool.submit(() -> {

    try {
        Thread.sleep(3000);
    } catch (InterruptedException e) {
        Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
    }

});

System.out.println(future.isDone());


Flow:

Task starts
    ↓
sleep(3 seconds)
    ↓
Main checks isDone()
    ↓
false ❌

The task has not finished yet, so: false
-------------------------
2. isDone() → true

Here we wait until the task finishes:

Future<?> future = pool.submit(() -> {

    System.out.println("Task completed");

});

future.get(); // get() : Wait until the task finishes, then give me its result."

System.out.println(future.isDone());

Output:

Task completed

true

Flow:

submit()
   ↓
Task executes
   ↓
Task finishes
   ↓
future.get() returns
   ↓
isDone()
   ↓
true ✅
---------------------
